[Music]  dino here  in this video we're going to cover  apogee tracing  if you haven't got a working api proxy  with api key verification  stop here and go back and view the prior  videos now  in the apogee ui select the proxy we  created previously  this proxy has the verify api key policy  let's use that to learn about tracing  select the trace tab  clicking this green button tells apigee  to begin collecting diagnostic  information for each request it receives  for the proxy  let's invoke the api again and we'll see  how that works  i want to make sure i pass a valid api  key  in the trace window you can see  immediately i have a trace record  for that request  exploring here i can see the properties  of the inbound request  and also the results of the verify api  key policy  i can also see the outbound request  being sent to the target  and what's this the api key is being  passed to the back end  that's because the apogee edge proxy is  passing through the request  unchanged if we want to avoid that  we can configure the proxy to modify the  request  to remove that query parameter let's do  that  in the preflow i'll add and assign  message policy a sign message  is a multi-purpose policy that can be  used to set or change  any part of a message normally  apogee edge propagates an exact copy of  the inbound message to the target  but with a signed message you can make  changes adding or removing headers  adding or removing query parameters  i'm going to configure this policy to  remove the query parameter  save the proxy flip back to the trace  tab  start a trace session  now invoke the api and flip back to  trace  and we can see the assigned message  policy is removing the query parameter  the proxy is no longer leaking that api  key to the back end  great apigee edge trace gives near  real-time diagnostic information to api  proxy developers during development  it will show you up to 20 transactions  now it's not intended to deliver a log  of transactions for that you can use the  message logging policy  in this video we use the trace facility  and we tried the assigned message policy  that's just one of the set of 30 plus  policies that are built into apogee edge  don't forget to learn more check out the  product documentation  and visit the community site to explore  further  be sure to watch the next video in this  series where we'll cover the api  developer portal  till next time keep it digital

